RadioListTile.doc:
A list row with a radio button, selected by a click anywhere on it. It must be inside a
`RadioGroup.Root`. The radio comes first unless `controlPosition` is `end`;
`secondary` fills the other side.

Chip.doc:
A compact element for an action, a filter, an entry or a suggestion, as high as a
button, with an outline and medium rounded corners:
- `assist`: an action, with an optional leading icon;
- `filter`: a toggle; while `selected` it fills with the secondary container color and
  shows a check mark;
- `input`: an entry such as a tag, with a remove button when `onRemove` is set;
- `suggestion`: a suggested reply or query.

Value.doc:
The label of the chosen option, or the `placeholder` while nothing is chosen. Without a
`collection` on the root, an option's label is known once the list has been opened;
pass `children` to show the value in your own way.

Handle.doc:
The grip of a sheet. Dragging it toward the sheet's edge closes a dismissible sheet;
on a bottom sheet with snap points it moves between them, and so do the Up and Down
arrows, while a click, Enter or Space cycles to the next height.
